00:51:53.105 --> 00:51:55.021
I don't understand him.


00:51:55.440 --> 00:51:57.314
What's "toke up"?


00:51:57.482 --> 00:51:59.357
I'll tell you later.


00:52:04.569 --> 00:52:05.816
Mrs Paulette...


00:52:08.570 --> 00:52:11.403
Do you know Granny Junkie well?


00:52:11.571 --> 00:52:13.153
"Granny Junkie"?


00:52:13.780 --> 00:52:16.114
Even her grandson, Léo.


00:52:16.322 --> 00:52:17.573
Her daughter, Agnès.


00:52:17.740 --> 00:52:19.947
And her son-in-law, a policeman.


00:52:26.367 --> 00:52:27.451
There you are.


00:52:28.452 --> 00:52:30.076
Thank you. Goodbye.


00:52:34.496 --> 00:52:35.870
Coming.


00:52:37.831 --> 00:52:39.038
Why are you here?


00:52:39.205 --> 00:52:40.164
We're pissed.


00:52:40.373 --> 00:52:41.538
Fuckin' A.


00:52:42.582 --> 00:52:44.040
Madam doesn't play cards.


00:52:44.209 --> 00:52:47.541
Or when she does, she falls asleep.


00:52:47.711 --> 00:52:50.002
What's your little secret?


00:52:50.961 --> 00:52:52.460
I sell cakes.


00:52:54.212 --> 00:52:59.130
Imagine "The Bold and the Beautiful"
on a TV like this!


00:53:01.923 --> 00:53:05.506
And you bought that
with the sale of your cakes?!


00:53:06.382 --> 00:53:08.300
Do you think we're stupid?


00:53:08.468 --> 00:53:10.718
No, I don't think you are.


00:53:10.925 --> 00:53:14.677
We thought we were your friends,
but if you don't trust us,


00:53:14.803 --> 00:53:16.219
